in order to see the future. {Ashihara did make a computer in order to see the future.}

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.680
But what he saw was a catastrophe. {But what he saw was a catastrophe.}

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.150
Catastrophe? {Catastrophe?}

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.020
Rodan! {Rodan!}

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:01.100
Wear this. {Wear this.}

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.170
The sky over England is turning red. {The sky over England is turning red.}

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:31.510
In addition to the Manda,
Rodan have been sighted over the sea. {In addition to the Mandas, Rodans have been sighted over the sea.}

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:34.510
The defense line has been set offshore
 and the shooting has commenced.{(レポーター)洋上に 防衛ラインが設置され狙撃が開始されました}

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:38.520
What kind of catastrophe did Professor Ashihara see? {What was the catastrophe Professor Ashihara saw?}{tlc}

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.580
He saw an error.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:41.270
An error? {-He saw an error. -An error?}

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:43.480
Pero 2, what's one plus one? {Pelops II, what's one plus one? (Pelops II, what's one plus one?)}

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:44.770
Two. {Two.}

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:46.440
Again.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:47.170
Two.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.280
Repeat it 100 million times. {Repeat it 100 million times.}

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.780
Done. It's still two. {Done. It's still two.}

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:55.200
What if the result was different each time? {What if the result was different each time?}

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:58.120
We usually conduct error corrections when they occur, {We usually conduct error corrections when they occur,}

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:01.440
thus I expect it to be
a hardware or software malfunction. {thus I expect it to be a hardware or software malfunction.}

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:05.790
It's normal to assume something's wrong,
but what if you can't find the problem? {It's normal to assume something's wrong, but what if you can't find the problem?}

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:09.590
There's no malfunction,
but you get a different answer each time... {There's no malfunction, but you get a different answer each time...}

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:12.300
It is possibly a lack of understanding of time. {It is possibly a lack of understanding of time.}

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:13.800
That's possible. {That's possible.}

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.970
Ashihara succeeded in applying time distortion {Ashihara succeeded in applying time distortion}

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:21.060
to calculate the result of something
a fraction of a second in the future. {to calculate the result of something a fraction of a second in the future.}

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:26.130
He then reached further into the future 
to enhance computing capacity. {He reached further into the future to enhance computing capacity.}

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:28.820
One, ten, even one hundred seconds into the future. {One, ten, one hundred seconds into the future.}

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:33.820
But from a certain point,
the results became inconsistent. {But from a certain point, the results became inconsistent.}

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:38.590
He couldn't figure out why. 
That's the Ashihara Catastrophe. {He couldn't figure out why. That's the Ashihara Catastrophe.}

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:42.330
Something like a collision with a black hole in the future? {Was it a collision with a black hole in the future? (Like a black hole in the future?)((銘)未来で ブラックホールに 衝突したとかですか?)(tlc, jes)}

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.580
He thought it was an anomaly in the laws of physics. {He thought it was an anomaly in the laws of physics.}

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.330
A twist in the laws of physics? {A twist in the laws of physics?}{歪む [ゆがむ, いがむ] (1) (v5m,vi) to warp; to bend; to contort (2) (v5m,vi) to be perverted; to be warped (of a view, mind, etc.); to be distorted; to be cross-grained}

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:50.590
Maybe more along the lines of mathematical fact. {Maybe more along the lines of mathematical fact.}

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:54.350
An incongruity of numbers? Like "6 = 9"? {An incongruity of numbers? Like "6 = 9"?}

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.930
There <i>is </i>a supercomputer. {There is a supercomputer.}

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:02.100
But it doesn't work properly
because it creates a catastrophe. {But it doesn't work properly because it creates a catastrophe.}

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:05.270
Isn't there a way to avoid it? {Isn't there a way to avoid it?}

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.970
That would be up to you.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:08.810
What?

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:14.610
Nobody understood his research,
but you're starting to decipher it. {Nobody understood his research, but you're starting to decipher it.}

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:18.010
You're closer to him than anybody else. {You're closer to him than anybody else.}

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.990
This is where he used to live. {This is where he used to live.}

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:24.790
Everything you see here are his research documents. {Everything you see here are his research documents.}

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:28.000
You brought me here for this? {You brought me here for this?}

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.360
That's what was in the photo. {That's what was in the photo.}

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:35.840
We first thought they melted in the heat,
but that wasn't the case. {We first thought they melted in the heat, but that wasn't the case.}

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:39.010
This was caused by the gas it exhaled... {This was caused by the gas it exhaled...}

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:42.060
You were only
supposed to break down red dust. {You were only supposed to break down red dust.}

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.680
That was the plan. {That was the plan.}

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.440
You could've destroyed SHIVA! {You could've destroyed SHIVA.}

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:48.730
But SHIVA is unharmed. {But SHIVA is unharmed.}

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.940
Restraining the research director? I'm appalled. {Restraining the research director? I'm appalled.}{tlc - aoi-chang...}

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:56.320
If it weren't for him, that monster would've gotten out. {If it weren't for him, that monster would've gotten out.}

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:59.130
The end doesn't justify the means. {The end doesn't justify the means.}

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:01.750
There's no room for decorum. {There's no room for decorum.}

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:07.540
Ashihara predicted that Archetype will
recreate the world in the 21st century. {Ashihara predicted that Archetype will recreate the world in the 21st century.}

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.580
That's an unfounded hypothesis. {That's an unfounded hypothesis.}

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:12.210
SHIVA is getting more active. {SHIVA is getting more active.}

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:18.340
Now that some of his work has been
deciphered, we daresay he wasn't crazy. {Now that some of his work has been deciphered, we daresay he wasn't crazy.}

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.970
I don't believe it. {I don't believe it.}

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:25.270
Li's co-researcher figured it out, 
so let's have a word with Li. {Li's co-researcher figured it out. Let's talk to Li.}

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:28.730
The board approved the relaunch
of Ashihara's experiments. {The board approved the relaunch of Ashihara's experiments.}

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.730
A robot! {A robot!}

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.400
I know! I saw it on TV. {Yes. I saw it on TV.}

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.070
Jumbo Jet! {Jumbo Jet!}

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:38.200
No, no! Jet Jumbo. {No. Jet Jumbo.}

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:39.700
Come here, Jet Jumbo. {Come here, Jet Jumbo.}

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:42.910
No. My name is Jet Jaguar. {No. My name is Jet Jaguar.}

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.080
Wow! It talks! {Wow! It talks!}

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.200
Do you have missiles? {Do you have missiles?}

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.750
Shoot a laser beam! {Shoot a laser beam.}

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.420
Can you fly? {Can you fly?}

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:58.550
It smells awful. {It smells awful.}

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:00.820
Eaten by its own kind? {Eaten by its own kind?}

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.260
Wrong. {No.}

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:05.260
It was Godzilla. Take a look at this. {It was Godzilla. Look at this.}

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.020
Teeth marks. {Teeth marks.}

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:09.980
Maybe it was sea roaches or squillas. {Maybe it was sea roaches or squillas.}

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:13.270
Sea roaches that can eat this giant in a few days? {Sea roaches that can eat this giant in a few days?}

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.020
Gigantic sea roaches?

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:17.610
He was home. He's taking the day off. {-Gigantic sea roaches? -He was home. He's taking the day off.}

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.320
What did he say about that? {What did he say about that?}

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:23.280
He had no idea.
He said everything was fine yesterday. {He had no idea. He said everything was fine yesterday.}

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:26.580
What is <i>that,</i> then? {So what is that?}

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:30.290
The gigantic sea roach's nest. {The gigantic sea roach's nest.}

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:32.710
Ready? One. {Ready? One.}

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:34.790
Ready? Three. {Ready? Three.}

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.070
Ready? Seven. {Ready? Seven.}

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.260
You won again? {You won again?}

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:41.200
You're cheating!

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.300
I am not cheating.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.970
What's he doing? {What is it doing?}

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.430
Hey! We have work to do! {Hey! We have work to do!}

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:47.680
Roger. {All right.}

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.770
Aw, you're leaving already? {You're leaving already?}

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:52.230
Sorry, but duty calls. {Sorry, but I have to work.}

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:55.900
Are you off to hunt kaiju? Good luck! {Are you going kaiju hunting? Good luck!}

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:57.190
Thanks. {Thanks.}

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:58.820
Let's play again! {Let's play again!}

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:01.700
Bye bye! See you later! {See you!}

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:01.700
Bye bye!

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:05.700
Were you playing a game? {Were you playing a game?}

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:09.160
I won ten times in a row. {I won ten times in a row.}

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:14.170
Then the bastard bristled 
its spikes and came chargin' at me! {Then it bristled its spikes and came charging at me.}

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:18.880
But my reactions were quick!
I dodged and jumped onto its back. {But I reacted quickly. I dodged and jumped onto its back.}

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:23.720
From there, I found a big spike 
from the bunch and hung onto it! {I found a big spike from the bunch and hung onto it.}{tlc - i feel like this is msissing something but i'm having trouble parsing the jp}{並ぶトゲから ふてえやつを見繕って捕まえたからには もう離さねえ}

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:27.930
It's really reassuring to have 
Outaki Factory's cooperation for this. {It's reassuring to have your cooperation.}

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:30.710
Heh. If anything happens... {If anything happens...}

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:34.810
I predicted which fingers they'd hold up
by their eye and muscle movement. {I predicted which fingers they'd hold up by their eye and muscle movement.}

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.270
Hey, that's cheating. {That's cheating.}

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:41.190
It's not against the rules.
You play games to win them, right? {It's not against the rules. You play games to win them, right?}

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:45.340
Winning isn't everything. Search Homo Ludens. {Winning isn't everything. Search Homo Ludens.}

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:49.200
Human culture was developed through play? {Human culture was developed through play?}

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.410
An unknown is approaching. {An unknown is approaching.}

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.790
An unknown? {An unknown?}

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:54.140
Be careful. {Be careful.}

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:02.130
What is it? Nothing's happening. {What is it? Nothing's happening.}

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:05.930
Incoming, eleven o'clock. It's getting closer. {Incoming, eleven o'clock. It's getting closer.}

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:06.890
There. {There.}

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.190
Up there! {Up there!}

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:30.450
It's a spider monster this time. {It's a spider monster this time.}

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:57.560
I hate spiders! {I hate spiders!}

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:00.860
Bam. {Bam.}

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.830
It's sliced in two but still moving... {It's sliced in two but still moving.}

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.250
Take this! {Take this!}

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.700
This ain't the time to let your guard down! {Don't let your guard down.}

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:25.630
Especially when it's tryin' to pick a fight! {Especially when it's been provoked.}

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:27.000
Lose a battle to win the—{Fight to the death...}{war}

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.840
Hey! Wretched monster! {Hey! Wretched monster!}

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:35.980
Whew, that was close! {I'm still alive.}

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:39.330
Is that our culprit here? {Did it make that?}

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:45.570
Looks a little too big to be a one-man job... {It looks too big for work done by one.}

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.450
I'll call for backup.

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:47.450
Six of them. {-I'll call for backup. -Six of them.}

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:50.240
We're surrounded. Stay alert. {We're surrounded. Stay alert.}

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:01.170
Jet Jaguar, can you stop them? {Jet Jaguar, can you stop them?}

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:02.810
Four at best. {Four at best.}

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:04.090
The other two? {The other two?}

00:17:04.090 --> 00:17:06.720
Run toward twelve o'clock at my signal. {Run toward twelve o'clock at my signal.}

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:07.730
All right. {All right.}

